# spi_hw_stream pinout for UPduino v3
#
# SCK / MOSI / CS keep the same pins uart_to_spi.v uses, but their
# DIRECTIONS are reversed: the FPGA is the slave here, so the master drives
# all three.  MISO is new — a slave needs its own data-out line and cannot
# share the master's MOSI — so it lands on gpio_13, the same pin
# host_to_spi.v already uses for MISO.
#
# These are the hard SPI IP's pads routed out through general fabric, not
# the UP5K's dedicated config-SPI pins (14/15/16/17).  That keeps the
# onboard flash and the FTDI programmer off this bus; pin 16 is still
# driven high to hold the flash deselected.

set_io -nowarn led_r        41
set_io -nowarn led_g        39
set_io -nowarn led_b        40

set_io -nowarn spi_cs_flash 16

set_io -nowarn spi_sck      11
set_io -nowarn spi_cs       19
set_io -nowarn spi_mosi     21
set_io -nowarn spi_miso     13
